From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BananaDS <bananads@localhost>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:39:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Arm64Emitter: CountLeadingZeros by CLZ, not bit by bit
 (MELONDS_JIT_SOFTCLZ)

IsImmLogical (the emitter's check for an AND/ORR/EOR immediate) counts leading zeros four times with Dolphin's
portable loop, a bit at a time: up to 64 rounds each. In Mario Kart DS's race start the JIT compiles ~4.5 new
blocks a frame and calls IsImmLogical only ~39 times a frame, but at ~1,100 instructions a call it was ~43k
instructions a frame of the emulator's thread (qemu), a fifth of the compiler's time. CountLeadingZeros(value, 64)
is now __builtin_clzll (64 for zero): the same count, so the same encodings and the same emitted code; only the
compiler gets faster. MELONDS_JIT_SOFTCLZ=1 keeps the loop.
---
 src/dolphin/Arm64Emitter.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/dolphin/Arm64Emitter.cpp b/src/dolphin/Arm64Emitter.cpp
index abb89a2..de39983 100644
--- a/src/dolphin/Arm64Emitter.cpp
+++ b/src/dolphin/Arm64Emitter.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 // Licensed under GPLv2+
 // Refer to the license.txt file included.
 
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <array>
 #include <cinttypes>
@@ -32,8 +33,20 @@ const int kWRegSizeInBits = 32;
 const int kXRegSizeInBits = 64;
 
 // The below few functions are taken from V8.
+// BananaDS patch 0088: MELONDS_JIT_SOFTCLZ=1 keeps the bit-by-bit loop below (up to 64 rounds, ~1,100 instructions
+// an IsImmLogical call in Mario Kart DS's race start); otherwise CLZ, which counts the same: the leading zeros of
+// the width's low bits, width for zero. Only the compiler's own speed changes: the code it emits is the same
+
 int CountLeadingZeros(uint64_t value, int width)
 {
+  // (read at the first call: the JIT's stubs, as the first compiler is created; one setting per process)
+  static const bool SoftCLZ = getenv("MELONDS_JIT_SOFTCLZ") && atoi(getenv("MELONDS_JIT_SOFTCLZ"));
+  if (!SoftCLZ)
+  {
+    // (every caller passes 64; another width takes the loop)
+    if (width == 64)
+      return value ? __builtin_clzll(value) : 64;
+  }
   // TODO(jbramley): Optimize this for ARM64 hosts.
   int count = 0;
   uint64_t bit_test = 1ULL << (width - 1);
